  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tautua: Samoa Human Development and Social Inclusion</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Tautua - Human Development for All program for Samoa builds on Australia&apos;s investments across human development sectors. It provides institutional strengthening support to Government and the community sector to improve the quality and inclusiveness of service delivery in relation to health, education, gender equality and disability inclusion. It focuses on four critical social issues: reducing non-communicable diseases; reversing stagnated leaning outcomes; reducing the vulnerability of those whose rights to exercise a choice and whose personal safety are threatened; and overcoming barriers to inclusive communities.</narrative>
  </description>
